# Always push when done

When a user-requested coding task is finished (feature, fix, or requested change):

1. Commit relevant source changes with a concise message (use `git -c user.name=... -c user.email=...` if repo has no user identity).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`git push origin HEAD`) without asking again.
3. Do this every time unless the user explicitly says not to push/commit.

Do not commit secrets, `.env`, or unrelated `dist/` / `node_modules` noise.
